Subject: [PATCH] Metal: expand JIT guard with compiler RSS and process limits

The published 0008 metal_jit_guard is a thin compile mutex. The measured tree
grows it into a process-aware guard: attribute MTLCompilerService RSS, enforce
compiler memory ceilings, poll metal/metallib child processes, and fail closed
(exit 86) when the offline toolchain footprint exceeds the safe limit.

Without this, concurrent offline metallib compiles can exhaust host memory and
wedge the measurement host. Env knobs (compiler memory limit, poll interval)
match the measured tree.

Source reproduction only: this patch was not compile-verified here.

